## Trim notes

The following bashkit modules/features were removed because `hq` does not use
them (see `.claude/plans/warm-twirling-stonebraker.md` for the extraction plan):

- Network builtins: `curl`, `wget`, `http`
- Remote access: `git`/`ssh` builtins (scp, sftp)
- Data stores: `sqlite`, `jq`
- Embedding runtimes: python, typescript (zapcode)
- Bot authentication / credential injection
- Snapshot/restore virtualization
- Interop layer (tokio bridge)
- Scripted tool / tool_def AI framework (bashkit's `BashToolBuilder`)
- Structured logging integration and trace collection
- Job control (`kill`/`wait` real-process builtins)
- Archive builtins (`tar`, `gzip`, `zip`) and exotic utilities (`parallel`,
  `retry`, `rg`, `semver`, `template`, `compgen`, `caller`, `fc`,
  `mapfile`, `watch`, `less`, `tree`)

All remaining behavior is identical to bashkit v0.12 for the features that
were kept.